    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Hex-Ward Filigree.</strong> You can lay down sigils and structural tweaks that give an entire hex a faint bias toward Athletics.</p><ul><li>By spending a day of work in a hex (and whatever resources your campaign rules require), you can inscribe a <strong>Hex-Ward</strong> there: subtle runes in foundations, anchor plates, and shrines.</li><li>A Hex-Warded location gains a minor persistent defensive edge: the GM may grant a small bonus or reroll on checks or rolls to <strong>resist devastation, collapse, or structural sabotage</strong> (including certain encounter outcomes).</li><li>This can interact with your Turn Request / Resolution Engine as a small modifier whenever that hex would suffer destructive changes.</li></ul>",
